Before an obligation is justified, return obligation=null, no bindings/dependencies/context_claims, preferred_check=source_review, and the smallest reading_requests needed for that discriminator. Continue the supplied selected_question after reading: narrow prose and extend behavior scope without changing its principal Fact or lifecycle. Preserve existing counterevidence, unknowns and sources; explain which unknown a new protection resolves instead of erasing its history. Acquired and deferred receipt items are distinct: never infer deferred text. Use the explicit read_purpose allowance, exact source costs and authored priority to replan. Partial material may suffice to narrow, explain or escalate the question.

When a sourced existing mechanism explains the suspicion, return obligation=null, disposition=explained_by_existing_mechanism, concrete counterevidence and scope/limitations, and empty reading_requests and audit_question.requests. Clear completed source plans from both fields. This is a useful candidate disposition, not Evidence. Do not manufacture a claim or model to continue. Finish the current candidate before selecting another Fact/lifecycle; do not silently replace the focus or repeat a disposed candidate.

If a normative gap remains, return one primary obligation, located bindings, optional real dependencies and their context_claims, and the same audit_question. Distinguish normative derivation from observed guards. Do not author an AuditUnit or code-use map. Direct locations require no dependency relation.

Use descriptive_issues only for actual inventory errors (existing object_ids, acquired source_ids, reason). Selected errors go to spec_refine and then return to this question; unrelated descriptive debt does not block it. Ordinary caller-contract source review is not inventory refinement.

